---
/**
 * BEYOND ACADEMICS → SPORTS & GAMES  ·  audit §4.
 *
 * ═══ THE ORDER IS THE CLIENT'S AND IS THE POINT OF THE PAGE ═════════════════
 *
 * The audit says the live page's emphasis "appears to be primarily on
 * achievements" and asks for it inverted. This page runs in exactly the client's
 * order, and it is written out here so a later edit cannot quietly reshuffle it:
 *
 *   1 Facilities     ivory · alternating rows, three photographic slots each
 *   2 Games          INK   · the highlight — a fifteen-card horizontal carousel
 *   3 Participation  — REMOVED at client instruction, see the note in the body
 *   4 Inter-house    sand  · the sticky ticket deck, house fixture → national
 *   5 Coaching       white · staggered tinted cards under a cloud edge
 *   6 Record        ivory · fourteen achievement blocks, each with its gallery
 *   7 Results       sand  · every published placing, pulled into one board
 *
 * §7 IS A CLIENT DECISION AND IT MADE §6 CONSISTENT. The placings used to live
 * inside two of the fourteen record blocks. Asmita's nine rows are a tournament
 * scoreboard — the school HOSTED that league, so the published field is mostly
 * other schools — which read as the school's own honours when it sat under the
 * school's own heading. Moved out, the results read as results, and all
 * fourteen blocks became the same object. See Results.astro.
 *
 * §6 IS THE LIVE PAGE'S OWN CONTENT, RESTORED. The client sent their original
 * Sports & Games page back and asked for its structure — a heading, the account,
 * and that achievement's own photographs — because the rebuild had reduced all
 * of it to six one-line records with no pictures. The Asmita league, both
 * national camps, the district handball sweep, UDAAN, the Annual Sports Day and
 * the four championship flyers were all missing. Sixty photographs came back
 * with them. See data/sportsRecord.ts.
 *
 * The audit's "achievements shown separately" is still honoured: §6 is the
 * SPORTING record and it comes last on the page, while the school-wide record —
 * robotics, innovation, third-party recognition, academics — lives at
 * /beyond-academics/achievements/, which the handoff band links to.
 *
 * ═══ THE RHYTHM ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * The ink beat at §2 is the highlight; the page then lightens through ivory,
 * sand and white before §6 returns to ivory for a long read, and the handoff
 * band closes on one dark card. Section padding is always the shared
 * `--sb-section-y`; a section that invents its own number breaks the rhythm.
 *
 * ⚠ TWO PHOTOGRAPHIC LIBRARIES, AND THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE.
 * `src/assets/` (JOSH GROUND, play ground, basket ball) holds twenty shots of
 * EMPTY grounds — no child plays a sport in any of them, which is why §§1-5 are
 * composed the way they are. `src/assets/sports-record/` holds sixty shots of
 * children actually competing, and belongs to §6. Do not use a §6 action shot to
 * illustrate a facility: it dates the facility to one fixture.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import SectionRail from '../../components/academics/SectionRail.astro';

import Facilities from '../../components/beyond/sports/Facilities.astro';
import GamesRail from '../../components/beyond/sports/GamesRail.astro';
import Ladder from '../../components/beyond/sports/Ladder.astro';
import Coaching from '../../components/beyond/sports/Coaching.astro';
import Record from '../../components/beyond/sports/Record.astro';
import Results from '../../components/beyond/sports/Results.astro';

import heroPhoto from '../../assets/JOSH GROUND/DSC_1287 copy.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={heroPhoto}
  />

  <SectionRail
    items={[
      { id: 'facilities', label: 'Facilities' },
      { id: 'games', label: 'Games' },
      { id: 'houses', label: 'Inter-house' },
      { id: 'coaching', label: 'Coaching' },
      { id: 'record', label: 'The record' },
      { id: 'results', label: 'Results' },
    ]}
  />

  {/* padding-block: 0 — every section carries its own --sb-section-y, and the
      panel adding its own on top is what put a 183px void under the hero on
      three earlier pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel sp-panel">
    <Facilities />
    <GamesRail />

    {/* ⚠ NO "STUDENT PARTICIPATION" SECTION — removed at the client's
        instruction. `Participation.astro` and its data are intact, so restoring
        it is one import and one tag.

        Worth knowing what went with it: audit 4.5 names student participation
        explicitly, alongside facilities, games, inter-house and coaching. Four
        of those five are still here; participation is the one now missing. */}

    <Ladder />
    <Coaching />
    <Record />
    <Results />

    {/* ⚠ NO "BEYOND THE FIELD" HANDOFF BAND HERE — removed at the client's
        instruction. It linked to /beyond-academics/achievements/ and named the
        three majors behind that link.

        NOTHING WAS DELETED: `AchievementsLink.astro` is intact, so restoring it
        is one import and one tag. Worth knowing what went with it — the page
        now ends on the results board with no route to the school-wide record,
        which is still reachable from the main navigation but no longer from
        here. */}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.sp-panel { padding-block: 0; }

  .sp-panel :global(section[id]) {
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--sb-masthead-h) + 24px);
  }

  /* The games rail is full-bleed ink and sits directly under the facilities
     section; without this the panel's rounded top corner clips its left edge on
     wide screens. */
  .sp-panel :global(.grail) { border-radius: 0; }
</style>
